2. In this Order, unless the context otherwise requires —
“appropriate film” means a classified film that is assigned under the Act a classification rating of “G”, “PG” or “PG13”;
“class licensee” means a person who is subject to a class licence by virtue of this Order;
“distribution outlet”, for a class licensee, means a place in Singapore —
(a)at which films are distributed by the class licensee in the course of any business (whether or not distributed with any thing else); and
(b)that is under the control (temporary or otherwise) or management of the class licensee;
“exempt unclassified film” means an exempt film within the meaning of the Films (Classification — Exempt Films Other than Video Games) Notification 2019 (G.N. No. S 338/2019);
“film” does not include a video game.
